This file lists code, data and protocol knowledge that irvis takes from other
projects, with their licences. Add an entry in the same pull request that adds
the material, in this form:

  <project name> (<URL>)
  Copyright (c) <year> <holder>
  Licence: <SPDX identifier>
  Used in: <paths in this repository>
  What: <what was taken: code, constants, a protocol description>

Third-party npm packages are not listed here, except the two below whose
licences ask for more than their notice. The web build carries the licence
texts of the npm packages bundled into it in THIRD-PARTY-LICENSES.md, next to
index.html (resources/web/ in the desktop packages); Electron and Chromium
ship theirs as LICENSE.electron.txt and LICENSES.chromium.html in the desktop
packages.

LeoDJ/P2Pro-Viewer (https://github.com/LeoDJ/P2Pro-Viewer)
Copyright (c) 2023 LeoDJ
Licence: MIT
Used in: packages/core/src/cameras/infiray-p2pro/, tools/capture-cli/src/usb-protocol.ts
What: protocol knowledge, no code: the USB ID 0x0bda:0x5830, the 256x384
  mode at 25 fps, and the split of the frame into an image half and a
  16-bit temperature half; the USB control-transfer sequences, mixed-endian
  TPD encoding, gain and palette commands reimplemented in TypeScript from
  P2Pro/P2Pro_cmd.py (revision 23887289d3841fdae25c3a11b8d3eed8cd778800).

atomic14/InfiRayCapture (https://github.com/atomic14/InfiRayCapture)
Copyright (c) 2025 atomic14
Licence: MIT
Used in: packages/core/src/cameras/infiray-p2pro/
What: a fact, no code: the conversion raw / 64 - 273.2, which confirms
  the divisor 64 (irvis uses the offset 273.15).

alufers/thermal-cat (https://github.com/alufers/thermal-cat)
Licence: none stated in the repository; only facts were taken, no code
Used in: packages/core/src/cameras/infiray-p2pro/
What: the raw value in 1/64 K (raw / 64 in kelvin), the 256x192 mode
  without temperature data, and the USB IDs.

